GL=[("Air gap","The space between the table or ground and the bottom of the coal bed. On the Slot Grill Compact it's 2⅞\" (3⅝\" on the Full Size), which helps minimize radiant heat to the surface below.","/small-patio-balcony-charcoal-grilling.html"),
("Ash over","When lit charcoal develops a light coat of gray ash on top. It's the sign the coals are ready to pour and cook on.","/how-to-light-charcoal-without-lighter-fluid.html"),
("Briquettes","Uniform pressed charcoal with binders. Steady, longer heat; more ash.","/best-charcoal-for-small-grills.html"),
("Carbon monoxide (CO)","A colorless, odorless, deadly gas produced by burning charcoal. The reason charcoal grills are only ever used outdoors in the open.","/power-outage-emergency-cooking-charcoal-grill.html"),
("Carbon steel","Steel made mostly of iron and carbon. Raw carbon steel is strong and holds heat well, and like cast iron it is seasoned to resist rust and release food.","/how-to-season-a-compact-grill.html"),
("Carryover cooking","The rise in internal temperature after food comes off the heat. Pull steaks a few degrees below target.","/reverse-sear-steak-small-grill.html"),
("Chimney starter","A metal tube that lights charcoal quickly and evenly using paper or starters underneath, with no lighter fluid.","/how-to-light-charcoal-without-lighter-fluid.html"),
("Cool zone","The thin or empty end of a two-zone fire, used to finish, hold and rescue food.","/two-zone-fire-on-a-small-grill.html"),
("Direct heat","Cooking right over the coals. Fast, high heat for searing and thin foods.","/charcoal-temperature-control-small-grill.html"),
("Dry brine","Salting meat ahead of time, uncovered, so it seasons deeper and the surface dries for a better sear.","/how-to-sear-on-a-charcoal-grill.html"),
("End pieces","The two short panels of a Slot Grill, with SLOT GRILL cut into the steel. On the Compact they're universal and face text-out.","/how-to-use-a-compact-charcoal-grill.html"),
("Flare-up","Flames caused by fat dripping onto hot coals. Move food to the cool zone instead of spraying water.","/two-zone-fire-on-a-small-grill.html"),
("Gauge","A measure of steel thickness; lower numbers are thicker. The Compact is 12-gauge, the Full Size 10-gauge.","/compact-vs-full-size-slot-grill.html"),
("Griddle (plancha)","A flat carbon steel cooking plate. The Slot Grill griddle is designed for the Slot Grill system and comes in half and full configurations.","/campfire-breakfast-griddle.html"),
("Hand test","Holding your palm over the grill to judge heat: about 2 seconds is high, 4–5 medium, 7+ low.","/charcoal-temperature-control-small-grill.html"),
("Indirect heat","Cooking beside, not over, the coals. Gentler heat for finishing and longer cooks.","/charcoal-temperature-control-small-grill.html"),
("Instant-read thermometer","A probe thermometer that reads internal temperature in seconds. The only reliable way to judge doneness.","/reverse-sear-steak-small-grill.html"),
("Lump charcoal","Wood charred into charcoal without binders. Lights fast, burns hot, less ash.","/best-charcoal-for-small-grills.html"),
("Polymerization","What happens when a thin film of oil is heated past its smoke point and bonds to steel as a hard, slick seasoning layer.","/how-to-season-a-compact-grill.html"),
("Re-seasoning","Stripping rust or flaky seasoning and rebuilding the coat with thin layers baked on.","/how-to-re-season-a-carbon-steel-grill.html"),
("Rest","Letting cooked meat sit before slicing so juices redistribute.","/reverse-sear-steak-small-grill.html"),
("Reverse sear","Cooking gently first, then searing at the end. Great for very thick steaks.","/reverse-sear-steak-small-grill.html"),
("Seasoning Balm","Slot Grill's balm for Full Size and Compact grills that creates a durable, non-stick protective coat on raw steel. Apply very thin; bake at 400°F for 1 hour.","/how-to-season-a-compact-grill.html"),
("Sear","High-heat browning that creates a crust and flavor.","/how-to-sear-on-a-charcoal-grill.html"),
("Side panels","The two long panels of a Slot Grill that lock into a tight V between the end pieces.","/how-to-use-a-compact-charcoal-grill.html"),
("Smash burger","A ball of beef smashed thin on a very hot flat surface for a lacy, crisp crust.","/smash-burgers-on-a-griddle.html"),
("Tab and slot","Slot Grill's tool-free, hinge-free construction: panels lock together by sliding tabs into cut slots.","/how-to-use-a-compact-charcoal-grill.html"),
("The Spine","A formed steel bottom on the Compact that gives a smooth, safe underside with no loose pieces to pinch your hand.","/how-to-use-a-compact-charcoal-grill.html"),
("Two-zone fire","A charcoal layout with a hot side and a cool side. The core technique of small-grill cooking.","/two-zone-fire-on-a-small-grill.html"),
("Waves","Cooking food in successive batches on a small grill, holding finished food safely while the next batch cooks.","/cooking-for-a-crowd-small-grill.html")]
page("glossary","Small Charcoal Grill Glossary","Plain-English definitions of charcoal grilling and Slot Grill terms: two-zone fire, ash over, gauge, air gap, tab and slot, the Spine, seasoning and more.",IMG["c08"],'<p>New to charcoal or to the Slot Grill? Here are the terms used across this site, in plain English, with a link to where each one matters most.</p>'+'<dl>'+"".join(f'<dt id="{html.escape(t.lower().replace(" ","-").replace("(","").replace(")",""))}"><b>{html.escape(t)}</b></dt><dd style="margin:0 0 1rem">{d} <a href="{u}">More →</a></dd>' for t,d,u in GL)+'</dl>',"howto",[("What is a two-zone fire?",GL[-2][1]),("What does ash over mean?",GL[1][1]),("What does steel gauge mean?",GL[12][1]),("What is tab and slot construction?",GL[-4][1])])

page("slot-grill-maker-story","The Slot Grill Story: Built in Texas, Refined by Real Cooking","How the Slot Grill came to be: a heavy-duty, tool-free, flat-pack carbon steel charcoal grill, made in Texas and sold direct by the maker. A note from Keith.",IMG["both02"],f"""
<p>The Slot Grill is made in Texas by Precision Cut Metals LLC, and it's sold direct by the people who make it. There's no middleman, no reseller network and no overseas factory. That's on purpose.</p>
<h2>The idea</h2><p>Most portable grills make a trade: light and flimsy, or sturdy and awkward. The Slot Grill set out to refuse that trade. Thick carbon steel that doesn't flex or warp, but cut so precisely that it assembles by hand with tabs and slots, no tools and no hinges, and packs flat enough to slide into a trunk, kayak, RV closet or camp box.</p>
<h2>Refined by use, not on a screen</h2><p>Slot Grill says the design didn't come from a computer screen or a rush to production. It was improved over years of real cooking: the team cooks on its own grills often, and each revision came from what performed best in actual cooking conditions.</p><p>That's where details like these came from:</p><ul><li><b>The Spine:</b> a formed steel bottom on the Compact, so the underside is smooth and safe with no loose pieces to pinch your hand.</li><li><b>The air gap:</b> 2⅞" between the table and the bottom of the coal bed on the Compact to help minimize radiant heat to tables, tailgates and decks.</li><li><b>Universal end pieces</b> with SLOT GRILL cut into the steel.</li><li><b>Two sizes:</b> the Full Size, and the Compact at 80% scale, still strong enough for cast iron.</li><li><b>A system:</b> griddles (planchas) designed alongside the grills to flat-stack properly and travel clean, plus a Seasoning Balm made for raw Slot Grill steel.</li></ul>
<h2>Texas big. Texas tough.</h2><p>Slot Grill's own words: "Texas big. Texas tough." The idea is a grill made to be used hard and to stay at your side for years. And: "No thin materials. No shortcuts."</p>
<h2>Seen by millions</h2><p>Slot Grill videos have been seen by millions, which is also why copies show up using the name and photos. Slot Grill® became a registered U.S. trademark of Precision Cut Metals LLC (Reg. No. 8,180,923), registered March 17, 2026, with first use August 14, 2024. Here's <a href="/real-slot-grill.html">how to spot a real one</a>.</p>
<h2>How Slot Grills are sold</h2><ul><li>Only at <a href="{SG}">SlotGrill.com</a>, the @SlotGrill TikTok Shop, and @SlotGrill on the Shop app.</li><li>No authorized third-party resellers.</li><li>Leaves the shop in 1–3 days, with free shipping in the lower 48.</li></ul>
<h2>What owners say</h2><blockquote>"This is an amazing American made product, I cant wait to use it again this weekend."<cite>George Ochoa, Compact owner</cite></blockquote><blockquote>"Well made looks like it's going to last for ages"<cite>Oscar Flores, Compact owner</cite></blockquote><p>The Compact averages 4.92 out of 5 from 77 reviews. <a href="/reviews.html">Read more reviews</a>.</p>
<h2>A note from the maker</h2><p>Thanks for cooking on a Slot Grill. This site exists to help you get the most out of yours: how to light it, control the fire, season and care for the steel, and cook great food wherever you take it. If you have a question or an idea, send it through the <a href="{CONTACT}">contact form</a>.</p><p>— Keith, Slot Grill</p>
{productbox("full")}
""","slot",[("Who makes the Slot Grill?","Precision Cut Metals LLC in Texas. Slot Grills are built and sold direct by the maker."),("Where is the Slot Grill made?","In Texas, USA."),("Does Slot Grill sell through resellers?","No. Slot Grill has no authorized third-party resellers; buy at SlotGrill.com, the @SlotGrill TikTok Shop or @SlotGrill on the Shop app."),("When was the Slot Grill trademark registered?","Slot Grill® was registered March 17, 2026 (U.S. Reg. No. 8,180,923), with first use August 14, 2024.")])
